      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, thanks, I wasn\u0027t sure how to trigger this code path.\n\nSimilar to generatePath(), we need to transform the drawable here -- and since there\u0027s no trivial way to achieve that, I ended up writing a matrix wrapper.  Maybe both paths and drawables should be transformed using the destination canvas in the calling code, so we can get rid of this?\n\nAnother couple of questions/observations:\n\n1) If I call setDrawable() in generateMetrics(), then generateDrawable() is never reached (presumably we\u0027re using the drawable already set on the glyph).  Is there a reason to prefer one over the other?\n\n2) When taking the drawable code path, I noticed the output is clipped to the drawable bounds.  When taking the image path, the output is implicitly clipped to the glyph bounds.  The two are not necessarily the same -- should the drawable case also clip to glyph bounds for consistency?",
      "parentUuid": "49dce6c9_bbef3374",
      "revId": "1eb7c70443372cdaa39f3bac422c3d7c1a97e0c2",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
